SPEC = {'file': 'cover_abtrace_data_scientist', 'label': 'Abtrace Data Scientist', 'center': True, 'paras': ['I am writing to apply for the Data Scientist position at Abtrace in London. I am completing an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. This role is unusually close to what I have actually done: building predictive models on large longitudinal health datasets to identify risk earlier.', 'What attracts me most to Abtrace is the focus on prevention in primary care, and that your algorithms are already used across more than 600 practices. My dissertation was on cardiovascular risk and lifestyle change, so identifying risk before patients become seriously ill is the problem I most want to work on. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, identifying what users actually need, and turning it into a workflow that can be tested and improved.', 'My longitudinal health data experience is direct. For my dissertation I used data from 458,840 UK Biobank participants, engineered multi-timepoint features and compared logistic regression with three tree-based ensembles for cardiovascular risk prediction, checking their calibration. I then used doubly robust causal forests on 71,428 participants, ran sensitivity analyses for timing, overlap and unmeasured confounding, validated the findings externally in NHEFS, and delivered the results as a deployed Streamlit application.', 'On transformer-based NLP, I also led a group project building a clinical NLP pipeline that parsed free-text radiology reports into structured features using fine-tuned transformer models, and evaluated where vision-language models failed against the text-derived signals. Before TikTok I worked as a Data Scientist Intern at DS Digital Technology on a medical AI engagement, where I built Python pipelines that called six LLM APIs with retrieval and multi-step workflows and automated the processing and scoring of over 2,400 records. I designed the evaluation framework around it, a 246-question benchmark and a six-dimension rubric that the client adopted as its acceptance standard, and I co-built a scientifically reviewed knowledge graph and ran blinded A/B tests to measure whether it actually improved output quality.', 'At TikTok Shop UK I am a Data Analyst Intern, where I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. Alongside my analytical work I built an AI agent that automates repetitive steps of the analytics workflow, which has been adopted by my own team and by partner teams. Building it meant understanding an existing workflow in detail, deciding which steps to automate, and then supporting colleagues as they began to rely on it. I use Claude Code in my development work and review the code it produces rather than accepting it unchecked.', "Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience with longitudinal health data, predictive modelling and clinical NLP could contribute to Abtrace's data science team. I am based in London. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029 without sponsorship."]}
